### Decision 29: Cross-Document Drift Reconciliation & Deterministic Settings Alignment

- **Date**: 2026-11-20
- **Status**: Accepted
- **Context**: 
  Following the Layer 2 pivot (Decision 26), multiple subtle schema divergences, retired field names, syntax discrepancies, and stale pre-pivot documentation references persisted across specification files, templates, and builder code.
- **Decision**:
  1. **Eliminated Retired `transform_handler`**: Replaced all remaining occurrences in `impl_doc_schema.md` (Sections 9, 10.2, 10.3, and Decision #16) with `processing.tools[].handler`.
  2. **Synchronized Blank `contract.yaml` Template**: Overwrote `templates/contract.yaml` to include `storage_mode: inline | claim_check`, `classification`, `tags`, `object` type with recursive `items.model_name` and nested `fields[]`, and `sla.latency.max_processing_seconds` matching Section 4.3 and Section 6 of `impl_doc_schema.md`.
  3. **Standardized Shared Component Syntax**: Unified on `processing.tools[].type: shared_component` in stage definitions, removed redundant `processing.shared_components[]` list, and centralized `usage_type` exclusively within `agent.yaml`.
  4. **Unified Array Items Syntax & 7-Contract Chain**: Replaced scalar `items: "string"` with typed object `items: { type: string }` across `spec_template.md`. Aligned stage IDs (`discover`, `plan`, `generate`, `dry_run`, `review`, `deliver`) and harmonized the complete 7-contract chain (`source_database_reference`, `source_schema_profile`, `transformation_plan`, `dbt_artifact_bundle`, `compilation_report`, `reviewed_artifact_bundle`, `delivery_manifest`) across `spec_template.md`, `impl_doc_schema.md`, and `builder.md`.
  5. **Deterministic BaseSettings & Framework Mixin**: Structured `src/core/config.py` into nested Pydantic models (`SourcesConfig`, `DestinationsConfig`, `DbtConfig`, `LLMConfig`) using `SettingsConfigDict(env_nested_delimiter="__")` so `${config.a.b.c}` maps 1:1 to `settings.a.b.c` without ad-hoc key flattening. Extracted `CHECKPOINTER_DB_URI` and `METADATA_DB_URI` into a shared `FrameworkRuntimeSettings` mixin.
  6. **Reconciled Pre-Pivot Documentation**:
     - In `impl_doc_schema.md` Section 7.2, replaced legacy Great Expectations checkpoints with Instructor Pydantic contract validators and native Layer 3 dbt generic tests (`unique`, `not_null`, `relationships`).
     - In `01_metadata_framework.md` Table `governance_audit`, replaced per-stage Python `pii_masking` with enterprise classification tagging and access policy evaluation.
     - In `approach.md`, added a historical note identifying it as a v0.4 genesis concept document and clarified that `spec.yaml` is retired post-build in favor of `impl_docs/*.yaml`.
- **Consequences**:
  - Ensures zero syntactic or semantic drift between spec templates, implementation documents, and generated Python code.
  - Guarantees deterministic environment variable injection and typed configuration binding for all generated Layer 2 agents.
  - Completely eliminates outdated references to Layer 3 batch ETL pipelines and retired schema constructs.
- **Reference**: [`impl_doc_schema.md`](file:///s:/DATA/agents/ddlc-agent-studio/design-docs/meta-agent/implementation-docs/impl_doc_schema.md), [`builder.md`](file:///s:/DATA/agents/ddlc-agent-studio/design-docs/meta-agent/builder.md), [`spec_template.md`](file:///s:/DATA/agents/ddlc-agent-studio/design-docs/meta-agent/input-spec-template/spec_template.md), [`contract.yaml`](file:///s:/DATA/agents/ddlc-agent-studio/design-docs/meta-agent/implementation-docs/templates/contract.yaml), [`approach.md`](file:///s:/DATA/agents/ddlc-agent-studio/design-docs/meta-agent/approach.md), [`01_metadata_framework.md`](file:///s:/DATA/agents/ddlc-agent-studio/design-docs/metadata-framework/01_metadata_framework.md)

